# Composite type annotation: record type via dict literal annotation syntax.
# A function annotated to accept a record with name: String, age: Number.
# The composite annotation resolves the dict literal [name: String age: Number]
# as a Record type via resolve_type_expr_value → resolve_type_expr → resolve_type_dict.
[describe: [fn [p@[type: [name: String age: Number] default: [name: "Alice" age: 30]]] p.name]
 result: [describe [name: "Bob" age: 25]]]
=== out
Dict({"describe": Function(p), "result": String("Bob")})
